This product includes software developed by Vadym Chernets, as part of Poly A1.

The kinds of personal data gatecall recognizes, and the check digits it uses for them, follow the
recognizers of Presidio (MIT License, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation; now maintained at
github.com/data-privacy-stack/presidio): payment cards with the Luhn check, IBANs with the ISO 13616
mod-97 check, and national identification numbers with each country's own check digit. The shapes of
API keys and tokens follow the public formats each vendor documents, as gitleaks (MIT License,
github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks) lists them. No Presidio or gitleaks code is copied: the recognizers in
skills/gatecall/scripts/detect.py are written anew in Python's standard library.

Rules of the program profiles (kimi, grok, agy) come from the Poly A1 track for companies (its plan,
section 0.6, step B13, and the council's late opinion opinions-late/meta-nb1.md:8).
